body:
When `c.ShouldBindJSON(&v)` is called with an empty body, it currently returns `EOF`. This is confusing because callers cannot distinguish an empty body from a truncated stream.

Expected: a clearly-typed error like `binding.ErrEmptyBody` (or wrap EOF with a descriptive message) so middleware can return a 400 with a meaningful message.

Reproduction:
```go
router.POST("/x", func(c *gin.Context) {
  var v struct{ Name string `json:"name"` }
  if err := c.ShouldBindJSON(&v); err != nil {
    // err is io.EOF here when body is empty
  }
})
```

This is an offline fixture used to demonstrate the agent without hitting the live GitHub API. Issue number is illustrative only.
